---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import RainfallChart from '../components/RainfallChart.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const nationalRain = release.observations.find(o => o.metricId === 'rainfall_departure_pct' && o.geographyId === 'india');
const hasRain = Boolean(nationalRain);
const nationalClaim = nationalRain && release.claims.find(c => c.id === nationalRain.claimId);
const centralRain = release.observations.find(o => o.geographyId === 'imd:central' && o.metricId === 'rainfall_departure_pct');
const eastRain = release.observations.find(o => o.geographyId === 'imd:east-northeast' && o.metricId === 'rainfall_departure_pct');
---
<Site title="A clearer view of India's water">
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">An independent evidence desk · India</p><h1>Water, in context.</h1><p class="lede">A place to examine rainfall, storage, groundwater, access and public response—one dated source at a time.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/explore/')}>Explore a place <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/methodology/')}>How we assess evidence</a></div></div><div class="hero-aside"><p class="eyebrow">Latest reviewed evidence</p>{hasRain ? <><p>{nationalClaim?.text} <a href={url(`/sources/${nationalRain?.sourceId}/`)}>National source ↗</a></p>{centralRain && eastRain && <p class="small">In a separate IMD graphic, Central India is reported at {centralRain.value}% and East & Northeast India at {eastRain.value}% for the same window. Regional cumulative normal totals were not printed, so those percentages have not been independently recomputed. <a href={url(`/sources/${centralRain.sourceId}/`)}>Regional source ↗</a></p>}</> : <p>Where do the latest available observations agree, diverge or leave us uncertain? A national verdict needs comparable data across several systems.</p>}<p class="small muted">A rainfall departure alone does not establish a national water crisis. Other systems remain unanswered.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><Status />{hasRain && <RainfallChart />}<div class="section-head" style="margin-top:3rem"><div><p class="eyebrow">National briefing</p><h2>What can we say now?</h2></div><p>{hasRain ? 'The rainfall snapshot is useful, but it cannot answer storage, delivery or health questions. Those systems need their own dated evidence.' : 'Current observations will appear here only after source retrieval, method checks and editorial review.'}</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><span class="tag">Rainfall</span><h3>Where and when did rain fall?</h3><p>Daily weather, season totals and long term normals answer different questions. The approved snapshot has its period and comparison period together.</p><a href={url('/explore/')}>Inspect coverage ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><span class="tag">Stored water</span><h3>What is available to use?</h3><p>Reservoir levels require a stable monitored group, usable capacity and matching dates. A national percentage alone cannot describe a city's supply.</p><a href={url('/understand/rain-to-tap/')}>Follow a drop ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><span class="tag">People</span><h3>Who can access water?</h3><p>Rainfall or tap connection counts do not establish reliable, safe household service. Local delivery and quality evidence need their own sources.</p><a href={url('/water-and-people/')}>Understand access ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="feature"><div><p class="eyebrow" style="color:#b8e6df">Explain the chain</p><h2>From the sky to a tap is a long journey.</h2><p>A rainfall signal may pass through catchments, rivers, reservoirs, aquifers, treatment and pipes. Each link has its own coverage and delay.</p><a href={url('/understand/rain-to-tap/')}>Follow a drop through the evidence ↗</a></div><div class="feature-graphic"><svg class="water-path" viewBox="0 0 430 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="diagram-title"><title id="diagram-title">Illustrative path from rainfall to household service, with uncertain links</title><path d="M50 120 H380" stroke-dasharray="5 7"/><circle cx="55" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="160" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="270" cy="120" r="29"/><circle cx="375" cy="120" r="29"/><text x="23" y="185">Rain</text><text x="128" y="185">Catchment</text><text x="235" y="185">Storage</text><text x="355" y="185">Tap</text></svg></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read deeper</p><h2>Four ways into the story</h2></div></div><div class="grid-2"><article class="editorial-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Place</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/states/')}>Start with a state or union territory</a></h3><p>Find the administrative place first, then see what is measured there and what remains unknown.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Time</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/history/')}>Compare the same season</a></h3><p>Historical resemblance is only meaningful when geography, cutoffs and measurement rules align.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Consequences</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/impacts/')}>Trace water through livelihoods</a></h3><p>Look for observed effects and documented coping, while keeping exposure separate from realized loss.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Next</p><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/outlook/')}>Watch the recovery signals</a></h3><p>Follow current official outlooks separately from observed rainfall, storage and service.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence desk</p><h2>Show the work.</h2><p>Every published measurement needs a source, date, unit, geography and method. Missing coverage is shown as missing; a build date never refreshes an old observation.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button" href={url('/sources/')}>Browse sources</a><a class="button button-light" href={url('/journalists/')}>Journalist desk</a></div></div><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Publication status</p><div class="numberline"><b>{release.observations.length}</b><span>approved observations in this build</span></div><div class="numberline"><b>{release.claims.length}</b><span>approved source-linked claims</span></div><p class="small">Counts describe the published snapshot, not the condition of India's water.</p></div></div></section>
</Site>
